Unbind a public definition from its module: s7_unshadow_global (TeXmacs)

TeXmacs binds a public definition (define-public) in its module and in
the rootlet, where the other modules find it. s7 caches, for each symbol,
the let of its latest local binding, here the module. A lookup walks out
from the current let, skips the lets which are newer than the cached one
and scans the slots of the others: from a module created before the
defining one (typically the module which loaded it), a lookup of the
public name scans that module and the user module (hundreds of slots) on
its way to the rootlet. Calls of public functions of other modules were
up to three times slower than calls in the same module.

The new C function s7_unshadow_global (let, symbol) removes the binding
of symbol in let and makes the symbol global again (id 0, local slot =
global slot), as if it had only been defined in the rootlet, so lookups
go straight there. It does so only when these two bindings are all the
bindings the symbol ever had (symbol_ctr 2): no other let can hold it,
and no lookup can be wrong. Otherwise it returns false and changes
nothing. TeXmacs registers it as (unshadow-global! let symbol) in
s7_tm.cpp and calls it in define-public (boot-s7.scm).

The debugging symbol_set_id checks that ids only grow, hence
symbol_set_id_unchecked.

--- a/s7.c
+++ b/s7.c
@@ -10663,6 +10663,31 @@
   return(let);
 }
 
+/* TeXmacs: the public definitions of the module system are bound in their module and in the
+ *   rootlet. The symbol then caches the id of the module, and the lookups from the other modules
+ *   scan the lets on their way to the rootlet (the user module has hundreds of slots). When these
+ *   two are the only bindings the symbol ever had, this removes the one in let and makes the
+ *   symbol global again, as if it had only been defined in the rootlet: the lookups go straight
+ *   there. With another binding (a parameter, a local variable, a second definition), a let might
+ *   still hold it, so nothing changes (false is returned).
+ */
+bool s7_unshadow_global(s7_scheme *sc, s7_pointer let, s7_pointer symbol)
+{
+  s7_pointer slot, last_slot = NULL;
+  if ((!is_let(let)) || (let == sc->rootlet) || (!is_symbol(symbol)) || (is_keyword(symbol)) ||
+      (symbol_ctr(symbol) != 2) || (!is_slot(global_slot(symbol))))
+    return(false);
+  for (slot = let_slots(let); is_slot_checked(slot); last_slot = slot, slot = next_slot(slot))
+    if (slot_symbol(slot) == symbol) break;
+  if ((!is_slot_checked(slot)) || (is_immutable_slot(slot)) || (local_slot(symbol) != slot))
+    return(false);
+  if (last_slot) slot_set_next(last_slot, next_slot(slot));
+  else let_set_slots(let, next_slot(slot));
+  set_local_slot(symbol, global_slot(symbol));
+  symbol_set_id_unchecked(symbol, 0);  /* is_global */
+  return(true);
+}
+
 
 /* -------------------------------- sublet -------------------------------- */
 static s7_pointer sublet_1(s7_scheme *sc, s7_pointer let, s7_pointer bindings, s7_pointer caller)
--- a/s7.h
+++ b/s7.h
@@ -447,6 +447,7 @@
 s7_pointer s7_sublet(s7_scheme *sc, s7_pointer env, s7_pointer bindings);   /* (sublet e ...) */
 s7_pointer s7_inlet(s7_scheme *sc, s7_pointer bindings);                    /* (inlet ...) */
 s7_pointer s7_varlet(s7_scheme *sc, s7_pointer env, s7_pointer symbol, s7_pointer value); /* (varlet env symbol value) */
+bool s7_unshadow_global(s7_scheme *sc, s7_pointer env, s7_pointer symbol); /* TeXmacs: see s7.c */
 s7_pointer s7_let_to_list(s7_scheme *sc, s7_pointer env);                   /* (let->list env) */
 bool s7_is_let(s7_pointer e);                                               /* (let? e) */
 s7_pointer s7_let_ref(s7_scheme *sc, s7_pointer env, s7_pointer sym);       /* (let-ref e sym) */
